weaknesses.value:
In terms of weakness, I think the first weakness is that some of the model assumptions seem to be very strong. For example, it is assumed that $\mathbb{E}[\Vert\hat{
abla}f(x)-
abla f(x)\Vert_{\ast}^{p}|x]\leq\sigma^{p}$. This assumption does not seem to hold in the simple setting of mini-batch. Is it possible to extend your analysis to allow the relaxation of this assumption to something like $\mathbb{E}[\Vert\hat{
abla}f(x)-
abla f(x)\Vert_{\ast}^{p}|x]\leq\sigma^{p}(1+\Vert x\Vert^{q})$ where $q$ can be related to $p$?

In your main result, i.e. Theorem 3.1., you mainly discuss the dependence on time $T$. What you obtained is $O(T^{ rac{2-2p}{3p-2}})$. However, there are other terms with explicit constants in your bound, and how does your bound depend on $p$? Does it have monotonic dependence on $p\in(1,2]$ or not? It seems to me that as $pightarrow 1$, the upper bound you have depends on whether $8\gamma/\sqrt{L\Delta_1}}$ and $\sigma$ are bigger than $1$ or smaller than $1$ and you will get very different results in these two cases. Is this something you expected and is there any intuition behind it?

